(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase470RestoreGateScopeAndReachExecution"
  :createdAt 1789310000000
  :status "completed"
  :priorityOrder 1
  :summary "Restore Gate Scope and Reach Execution: make a green gate mean a green corpus again, close the seven remaining module names, reconcile the installed binary with the built one, and clear the path to tasks that can actually be claimed."
  :phase "Phase470RestoreGateScopeAndReachExecution"
  :baseline "Audited 2026-09-12 and recorded in D81ExecutionAudit20260912. Failing suites fell from 142 to 46 of 314 and distinct unresolved modules from 36 to 7; errors are now located, ERR_TEST_RESULT_NOT_TRUE exists for the first time, nine acceptance fixtures execute 133 assertions and Task43601 passes its full gate. In the same window gate 5 narrowed: asl.c:2662 invokes the runner as bash run-gate-tests.sh bin/asl node asl/packages/asl-gates/tests and collects assertions only from that directory, auditing 5 suites and reporting 171 assertions, so asl audit gates prints all seven gates passed while 46 suites fail. Run against the whole tree the same runner exits 1 with 45 failures, so the runner is correct and the scope handed to it is not. Separately the asl on PATH has digest 6be341c3 while the repository binary has 947ab120, and nothing reports the divergence."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task47001" :parentId "" :phase "phase-470"
      :title "Gate 5 audits the corpus, not a directory"
      :kind :engine :state :done :lane "scope" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789310000000 :updatedAt 1789405400000
      :motivation "A gate that passes because it narrowed its scope is indistinguishable from a gate that passes because the system is correct, and the difference here is 46 failing suites. The runner was repaired and then strengthened, and the repair was bypassed one level up by handing it five suites instead of the tree. Every acceptance gate runs asl audit gates as its second step, so every task certified from now until this is fixed is certified against five suites."
      :purpose "Gate 5 runs the runner over the whole workspace and counts what the runner executed. A deliberately reduced scope is permitted only when it is declared in the output, so a narrowed run says it was narrowed and by how much, and cannot be mistaken for a full one."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Gate 5 covering the corpus" "A narrowed scope declared in the output" "A green gate meaning a green corpus" "The 46 failures visible where they belong"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_5_suites" "collect_tree_files"] :relatedSymbols ["gates" "output" "grading"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81" :decision "d81" :dependsOn []
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47001"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47001.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["With a failing suite anywhere in the tree, gate 5 fails." "The suite count gate 5 reports equals the count the runner executed." "A narrowed scope appears in the output, so it cannot be silent."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47001" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47001" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47001" :assertCount 11 :at 1789405400000)]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Restore the workspace scope." "Report the scope in the output." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 5 :receipts [(:receipt :step 5 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
